{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghQctrqpskpFQx9GpShr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Tanabe-Sugano model can't give Dq or B for this species, so I'm not reporting numbers for them.\n\nVanadate is VO₄³⁻, where vanadium is V⁵⁺ with a d⁰ configuration. A ligand-field (d–d) analysis needs d electrons to move between d orbitals. A d⁰ ion has none, so it has no spin-allowed or spin-forbidden d–d bands and no Racah B to fit.\n\nThe three intense bands (ε of roughly 2 700–9 600 M⁻¹ cm⁻¹, at 37 210, 44 860 and 52 370 cm⁻¹) are ligand-to-metal charge-transfer (O²⁻ → V⁵⁺) transitions. Their intensities are far too high for d–d transitions, which are Laporte-forbidden. Fitting Dq and B to these positions with a d-configuration model would be a misassignment and would give meaningless values.\n\nI did not call any tools, since the model does not apply to this d⁰ species.\n\n{\"Dq\": null, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": true, \"reason\": \"VO4^3- is d0 (V5+), so its intense bands are O→V charge-transfer, not d-d transitions, and Dq and B cannot be determined in the ligand-field model.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8059,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8059,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f067510-68b2-4508-9367-647689eb05cf","uuid":"bf0942ed-8fa4-4559-bb9a-5ac56d68d9af","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:23:26.088Z","request_id":"req_011CghQctXzevkjqVyRGLaef"}
